 forms'","src/rebar/_deprecations.py:98-99 registry note: 'honored as ALIASES (warn + map) rather than hard-removed: this is the sanctioned retirement path (there is no lib tombstone kind)'","src/rebar/_deprecations.py:141-143: a removed CLI verb / library function / MCP tool 'simply stops existing … No TOMBSTONE row: the tombstone registry only covers env/cfg/file inputs'","ABSENCE: no sentence in Approach explains why deletion (not a tombstone) fits these three surfaces, so an implementer choosing between the two removal mechanisms the module offers has no stated anchor."],"finding":"The Approach specifies WHAT to do (delete the rows, require canonical forms) and correctly preserves the custom-endpoint Chat Completions distinction, but states no POSITIVE rationale for WHY plain registry deletion is the right removal mechanism here — even though the same module maintains a separate tombstone registry (_TOMBSTONE_REGISTRY / RemovedInput) for removed inputs, and its own docstring draws the line at env/cfg/file inputs vs other surfaces.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff50d4ab39d253669","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section","norm_id":"nea177519b0807238","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer, seeing REMOVED inputs elsewhere routed through the tombstone registry, wrongly adds RemovedInput tombstones for the lib force params / openai-chat prefix — a kind the tombstone registry explicitly does not cover."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"In Approach, after 'Delete the scheduled aliases…', add: 'Use plain alias-registry deletion (remove the rows AND their emission/parse call-sites), not the tombstone registry: the tombstone registry (RemovedInput) covers only env/cfg/file inputs, whereas these are library kwargs and a provider-prefix, which per src/rebar/_deprecations.py simply stop existing.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes